  "notes": "FORMATION:\n{口|こう} (mouth) + {論|ろん} (argument, discussion) → verbal argument\n\nVERB FORM:\n{口論|こうろん}する (to argue, to quarrel)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {喧嘩|けんか} (fight, quarrel - can include physical)\n- {言|い}い{争|あらそ}い (verbal dispute)\n- {論争|ろんそう} (debate, controversy - more formal)\n- {揉|も}め{事|ごと} (trouble, dispute)\n- {口喧嘩|くちげんか} (verbal fight)\n\nDISTINCTION:\n{口論|こうろん} is specifically verbal and somewhat formal. {喧嘩|けんか} is more casual and can include physical fighting. {口喧嘩|くちげんか} is a casual word specifically for verbal fighting.",
